{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0123UdcCWc35ZwQtEMjkcJXk","type":"tool_result","content":"{\r\n  \"id\": \"US-173\",\r\n  \"title\": \"Implement A/B testing with Vercel Feature Flags and Edge Config\",\r\n  \"priority\": \"medium\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Set up Vercel Feature Flags using Edge Config to run server-side A/B tests on the /book page hero CTA and room card layouts without client-side flicker or layout shift. Edge Config reads are under 1ms p99 globally, making flags safe to evaluate in Next.js Middleware. Start with a CTA copy test to measure booking conversion impact scientifically.\",\r\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\r\n    \"Vercel Edge Config store created and connected to the project\",\r\n    \"@vercel/edge-config and @vercel/flags packages installed\",\r\n    \"A/B flag defined for /book page primary CTA copy (e.g., 'Book Now' vs 'Check Availability' vs 'Get Best Price Direct')\",\r\n    \"Flag evaluated in Next.js Middleware and variant cookie set before page render — zero layout shift\",\r\n    \"GA4 custom dimension records which variant each session received for statistical analysis\",\r\n    \"Vercel Flags UI in dashboard shows flag status, rollout percentage, and per-user override capability\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"technicalNotes\": [\r\n    \"Install: npm install @vercel/edge-config @vercel/flags\",\r\n    \"Read flag in middleware.ts: import { get } from '@vercel/edge-config'; const variant = await get('cta-variant')\",\r\n    \"Pass variant via x-variant response header or cookie to Server Component for conditional rendering\",\r\n    \"Flags as Code pattern: define flag types in flags.ts, resolve server-side only to prevent client exposure\",\r\n    \"Reference: https://vercel.com/docs/feature-flags, https://vercel.com/docs/edge-config\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"dependencies\": [],\r\n  \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\r\n  \"passes\": false,\r\n  \"model\": \"haiku\",\r\n  \"_skipped\": true,\r\n  \"_skipReas