{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JYLzTNoB9DaCYKvErPGfRC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see! Story US-173 is about implementing A/B testing with Vercel Feature Flags and Edge Config. The story has been marked as skipped with a note that it consistently produced oversized diffs (12854 lines, which is way over the 500 line limit).\n\nLooking at the story, the issue is likely that implementing Vercel Edge Config and flags is triggering unwanted dependencies or large file changes. Let me analyze what needs to be done:\n\n1. Install `@vercel/edge-config` and `@vercel/flags` packages\n2. Create/configure Edge Config store\n3. Define an A/B flag for /book page CTA copy\n4. Evaluate flag in middleware.ts\n5. Pass variant via cookie or header\n6. Add GA4 custom dimension for tracking\n7. Ensure Vercel Flags UI shows in dashboard\n\nThe problem is likely that:\n- Installing packages might trigger large lock file changes\n- Or the implementation might be trying to touch too many files\n\nGiven the prior crashes and oversized diffs, I need to:\n1. Be very minimal in my approach\n2. Only touch essential files\n3. Use uv instead of npm (per CRITICAL rules)\n4. Focus on core implementation without extra features\n\nLet me first understand the current state of the project by reading the key files.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":759,"cache_read_input_tokens":83972,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":759},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbfb22f1-8001-4265-ba1a-7ef245a7d994","uuid":"78fc8cfc-9f10-44ae-8ae7-1a6bae80d793"}
